WEBVTT

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.528
Welcome to this Java tutorial, where you'll

00:00:03.528 --> 00:00:06.242
learn to validate form input before saving

00:00:06.242 --> 00:00:08.956
state, explain errors clearly, and support

00:00:08.956 --> 00:00:11.605
consistent mouse and keyboard submission.

00:00:12.251 --> 00:00:15.179
These skills help applications accept useful

00:00:15.179 --> 00:00:18.173
requests while protecting previously accepted

00:00:18.173 --> 00:00:20.901
data when a person makes an invalid edit.

00:00:21.545 --> 00:00:24.549
A campus equipment desk accepts quantities from

00:00:24.549 --> 00:00:25.635
one through five.

00:00:25.635 --> 00:00:28.447
We'll build an order form that starts with a

00:00:28.447 --> 00:00:30.939
proposed three, then restore the course

00:00:30.939 --> 00:00:32.920
example's starting text of two.

00:00:33.562 --> 00:00:36.544
We'll submit a valid request, inspect two kinds

00:00:36.544 --> 00:00:39.400
of rejection, and recover with a valid entry.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.811
The window should explain each result.

00:00:41.811 --> 00:00:44.412
The notebook's separate model checks will

00:00:44.412 --> 00:00:46.887
establish which quantity remains saved.

00:00:47.617 --> 00:00:50.604
We'll write Main.java in the Workspace and use

00:00:50.604 --> 00:00:53.072
the supplied standalone JavaFX runner.

00:00:53.072 --> 00:00:55.994
The notebook uses its supplied Fx support for

00:00:55.994 --> 00:00:58.072
the same interface instructions.

00:00:58.072 --> 00:01:01.189
Start with the imports for the window, controls,

00:01:01.189 --> 00:01:03.267
layout, and event-handler types.

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:41.222
First define QuantityModel, the ordinary object

00:01:41.222 --> 00:01:42.840
that owns accepted state.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.624
Its private quantity starts at zero to mean

00:01:45.624 --> 00:01:47.112
nothing has been saved.

00:01:47.112 --> 00:01:49.831
Zero is an initial marker, not an accepted

00:01:49.831 --> 00:01:50.349
request.

00:01:50.349 --> 00:01:53.003
A getter exposes the saved number without

00:01:53.003 --> 00:01:55.980
allowing callers to assign the field directly.

00:02:09.198 --> 00:02:11.770
The save method receives proposed text.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:14.737
A candidate is a temporary value we can check

00:02:14.737 --> 00:02:16.781
before changing accepted state.

00:02:16.781 --> 00:02:19.617
Inside try, trim the surrounding spaces and

00:02:19.617 --> 00:02:21.200
attempt integer parsing.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.365
A valid integer can still be outside the allowed

00:02:24.365 --> 00:02:26.673
range, so that decision comes next.

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:51.290
The outside-range condition uses or: reject a

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:53.473
candidate below one or above five.

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:56.234
Returning from this branch leaves the saved

00:02:56.234 --> 00:02:57.261
field unchanged.

00:02:57.261 --> 00:02:59.444
We have not assigned quantity yet.

00:02:59.444 --> 00:03:02.269
A parsed zero reaches this decision, while a

00:03:02.269 --> 00:03:04.966
word cannot reach it because parsing fails

00:03:04.966 --> 00:03:05.351
first.

00:03:05.405 --> 00:03:08.128
Only an accepted candidate should replace

00:03:08.128 --> 00:03:08.726
quantity.

00:03:08.726 --> 00:03:10.718
Then return a success message.

00:03:10.718 --> 00:03:12.843
If integer parsing failed, catch

00:03:12.843 --> 00:03:15.965
NumberFormatException and return a whole-number

00:03:15.965 --> 00:03:17.227
correction instead.

00:03:17.227 --> 00:03:20.282
Neither rejection path should assign the saved

00:03:20.282 --> 00:03:20.680
field.

00:03:37.831 --> 00:03:40.519
Validation before mutation means checking a

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:42.956
proposal before replacing stored state.

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:45.956
Here, one assignment sits after the range check.

00:03:45.956 --> 00:03:48.893
The catch handles text such as a word, an empty

00:03:48.893 --> 00:03:51.393
string, or an integer too large for int.

00:03:51.393 --> 00:03:54.331
The method expects non-null field text; it does

00:03:54.331 --> 00:03:56.831
not define a separate null-input policy.

00:03:56.879 --> 00:03:59.909
Next enter the supplied Application start method

00:03:59.909 --> 00:04:01.676
and construct a fresh model.

00:04:01.676 --> 00:04:04.643
Add a persistent Quantity label and a TextField

00:04:04.643 --> 00:04:05.969
beginning with three.

00:04:05.969 --> 00:04:08.935
A TextField is an editable single-line control.

00:04:08.935 --> 00:04:11.965
Its value remains a String even when the visible

00:04:11.965 --> 00:04:13.354
characters are digits.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:50.078
The field's initial three is only a proposed

00:04:50.078 --> 00:04:52.868
request; creating or editing it does not save

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:53.612
that number.

00:04:53.612 --> 00:04:56.588
Associate the visible label with its field using

00:04:56.588 --> 00:04:57.331
setLabelFor.

00:04:57.331 --> 00:05:00.121
Then create wrapping status text and the Save

00:05:00.121 --> 00:05:01.113
quantity button.

00:05:01.113 --> 00:05:04.089
The label should remain visible after the person

00:05:04.089 --> 00:05:05.825
changes or clears the input.

00:05:23.296 --> 00:05:26.127
Control label association records which input

00:05:26.127 --> 00:05:27.385
the label describes.

00:05:27.385 --> 00:05:30.153
It complements visible placement rather than

00:05:30.153 --> 00:05:31.851
replacing keyboard testing.

00:05:31.851 --> 00:05:34.179
The status begins with Nothing saved.

00:05:34.179 --> 00:05:36.884
Visible validation feedback will later show

00:05:36.884 --> 00:05:39.840
either success or a useful correction sentence,

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:42.671
so the result does not depend on color alone.

00:05:42.721 --> 00:05:45.330
Submission is the deliberate request to read

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:47.524
current field text and try saving it.

00:05:47.524 --> 00:05:49.421
We'll create one submit handler.

00:05:49.421 --> 00:05:52.089
EventHandler is JavaFX's functional interface

00:05:52.089 --> 00:05:54.876
for event handling, and ActionEvent is the type

00:05:54.876 --> 00:05:57.070
of notification this handler accepts.

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:59.738
The lambda reads the field when invoked, asks

00:05:59.738 --> 00:06:02.347
the model to save, and displays the returned

00:06:02.347 --> 00:06:02.821
message.

00:06:21.937 --> 00:06:24.462
The declaration supplies behavior without

00:06:24.462 --> 00:06:25.386
submitting now.

00:06:25.386 --> 00:06:28.035
Both registrations refer to the same submit

00:06:28.035 --> 00:06:30.745
variable: button activation and Enter in the

00:06:30.745 --> 00:06:32.592
field call that same behavior.

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:34.379
Each call reads current text.

00:06:34.379 --> 00:06:37.335
Reading the field only during construction would

00:06:37.335 --> 00:06:39.737
keep an old value and miss later edits.

00:06:39.807 --> 00:06:42.535
Arrange the field label, input, button, and

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:43.613
status in a VBox.

00:06:43.613 --> 00:06:46.658
Use gap twelve and padding twenty, then show the

00:06:46.658 --> 00:06:48.497
Equipment Order window with a

00:06:48.497 --> 00:06:51.098
four-hundred-twenty by two-hundred-eighty

00:06:51.098 --> 00:06:51.923
content area.

00:06:51.923 --> 00:06:54.523
The final print reports the initial model

00:06:54.523 --> 00:06:56.807
quantity; it is outside the handler.

00:07:27.965 --> 00:07:30.801
Finish the supplied start and main methods.

00:07:30.801 --> 00:07:33.307
Launch begins this standalone program.

00:07:33.307 --> 00:07:35.747
Its short callbacks run on the JavaFX

00:07:35.747 --> 00:07:37.000
Application Thread.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.836
They perform the parse, model decision, and

00:07:39.836 --> 00:07:42.606
visible update without waiting for another

00:07:42.606 --> 00:07:43.265
operation.

00:07:51.882 --> 00:07:54.714
Click Run and inspect the difference between

00:07:54.714 --> 00:07:56.645
proposed text and saved state.

00:07:56.645 --> 00:07:59.670
The field should display three while the status

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:01.279
still says Nothing saved.

00:08:01.279 --> 00:08:03.982
The initial console report should be zero.

00:08:13.492 --> 00:08:16.173
The real Equipment Order window shows the

00:08:16.173 --> 00:08:19.247
persistent Quantity label, proposed three, Save

00:08:19.247 --> 00:08:21.078
quantity, and Nothing saved.

00:08:21.078 --> 00:08:24.217
We'll click Save quantity to request submission.

00:08:27.701 --> 00:08:29.442
The feedback is Saved three.

00:08:29.442 --> 00:08:32.239
The handler read the field at activation, and

00:08:32.239 --> 00:08:34.291
the model accepted the candidate.

00:08:34.291 --> 00:08:36.716
Now replace the proposed text with cat.

00:08:36.716 --> 00:08:39.203
Editing the field alone should leave the

00:08:39.203 --> 00:08:41.876
existing feedback until another submission.

00:08:52.081 --> 00:08:54.906
The field now contains cat while the status

00:08:54.906 --> 00:08:57.008
still shows the earlier success.

00:08:57.008 --> 00:08:59.571
This separates editing from submission.

00:08:59.571 --> 00:09:02.527
Click Save quantity to ask the model to check

00:09:02.527 --> 00:09:03.381
the new text.

00:09:06.875 --> 00:09:09.015
The whole-number correction appears.

00:09:09.015 --> 00:09:11.630
Integer parsing rejected the word before the

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:12.521
range decision.

00:09:12.521 --> 00:09:15.315
The source returns from catch without assigning

00:09:15.315 --> 00:09:15.850
quantity.

00:09:15.850 --> 00:09:18.703
That explains preservation of the earlier value,

00:09:18.703 --> 00:09:21.437
but the error label alone does not inspect the

00:09:21.437 --> 00:09:24.230
private field; use the notebook's getter checks

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:25.300
for that evidence.

00:09:35.489 --> 00:09:37.693
Zero produces the range correction.

00:09:37.693 --> 00:09:40.464
It can be parsed as an int, but it is not an

00:09:40.464 --> 00:09:41.597
accepted quantity.

00:09:41.597 --> 00:09:44.557
Both rejection paths preserve state by avoiding

00:09:44.557 --> 00:09:45.249
assignment.

00:09:45.249 --> 00:09:47.957
Now enter five and keep focus in the field.

00:09:47.957 --> 00:09:50.791
Pressing Enter should use the same submission

00:09:50.791 --> 00:09:52.239
behavior as the button.

00:10:00.889 --> 00:10:02.604
Enter displays Saved five.

00:10:02.604 --> 00:10:05.505
The form still accepts a valid request after

00:10:05.505 --> 00:10:05.967
errors.

00:10:05.967 --> 00:10:09.066
Focus matters: Enter here belongs to the field;

00:10:09.066 --> 00:10:12.232
Tab can move to the button, where Space requests

00:10:12.232 --> 00:10:12.957
its action.

00:10:12.957 --> 00:10:16.122
The two registered routes share the model's rule

00:10:16.122 --> 00:10:17.639
and feedback operation.

00:10:17.771 --> 00:10:20.851
Close this window before restoring the course

00:10:20.851 --> 00:10:21.398
example.

00:10:21.398 --> 00:10:23.588
The standalone process finishes.

00:10:23.588 --> 00:10:26.599
A complete new run creates another model and

00:10:26.599 --> 00:10:29.679
controls; it does not reuse the earlier saved

00:10:29.679 --> 00:10:30.021
five.

00:10:34.287 --> 00:10:37.548
Restore the TextField's starting text to two and

00:10:37.548 --> 00:10:39.857
the window title to Quantity Form.

00:10:39.857 --> 00:10:43.050
Keep the model, accepted range, shared handler,

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:44.476
and layout unchanged.

00:10:44.476 --> 00:10:47.737
Changing starting text still does not submit it.

00:11:00.077 --> 00:11:02.954
Predict the initial console report, field text,

00:11:02.954 --> 00:11:04.301
and status separately.

00:11:04.301 --> 00:11:06.872
Then trace button submission of two, Enter

00:11:06.872 --> 00:11:09.627
submission of cat, button submission of zero,

00:11:09.627 --> 00:11:11.402
and Enter submission of five.

00:11:11.402 --> 00:11:14.218
Which decisions reject, and when can the saved

00:11:14.218 --> 00:11:15.014
field change?

00:11:15.014 --> 00:11:17.340
Pause and record your reasoning before

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:17.952
observing.

00:11:26.188 --> 00:11:29.153
Run the restored source and compare the actual

00:11:29.153 --> 00:11:31.538
Quantity Form with those predictions.

00:11:40.145 --> 00:11:43.065
The form starts with proposed two and Nothing

00:11:43.065 --> 00:11:45.530
saved, while the console reports zero.

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:48.580
Click Save quantity for the first request, then

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:51.045
submit cat through Enter in the field.

00:12:07.044 --> 00:12:09.940
The word receives the whole-number correction

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:10.841
through Enter.

00:12:10.841 --> 00:12:13.544
The button and field use the same handler.

00:12:13.544 --> 00:12:16.376
Now submit zero with the button, followed by

00:12:16.376 --> 00:12:19.465
five with Enter, to compare range rejection with

00:12:19.465 --> 00:12:20.044
recovery.

00:12:39.239 --> 00:12:42.350
The range correction was followed by Saved five.

00:12:42.350 --> 00:12:45.332
A status message is the latest feedback, not a

00:12:45.332 --> 00:12:47.341
live view of every model field.

00:12:47.341 --> 00:12:49.869
The initial console zero also remains a

00:12:49.869 --> 00:12:51.165
construction report.

00:12:51.165 --> 00:12:53.887
Separate model tests in the notebook check

00:12:53.887 --> 00:12:56.739
stored quantity after each rejected request.

00:12:56.837 --> 00:12:59.697
Close the window and run the unchanged source

00:12:59.697 --> 00:13:00.332
once more.

00:13:00.332 --> 00:13:03.382
Its new model should return to the nothing-saved

00:13:03.382 --> 00:13:06.369
marker, even though the earlier window finished

00:13:06.369 --> 00:13:08.212
with a successful submission.

00:13:20.834 --> 00:13:24.059
The fresh Quantity Form again shows proposed two

00:13:24.059 --> 00:13:26.948
and Nothing saved, with the initial console

00:13:26.948 --> 00:13:27.754
report zero.

00:13:27.754 --> 00:13:30.912
That is complete recreation, not a reset of the

00:13:30.912 --> 00:13:31.517
old form.

00:13:31.517 --> 00:13:34.272
Close this last window after checking its

00:13:34.272 --> 00:13:34.809
display.

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:41.215
You separated proposed text, validation

00:13:41.215 --> 00:13:44.065
feedback, and accepted state, then tested shared

00:13:44.065 --> 00:13:45.846
mouse and keyboard submission.

00:13:45.846 --> 00:13:48.517
For another campus form, what must be checked

00:13:48.517 --> 00:13:51.307
before assignment, and how would you prove that

00:13:51.307 --> 00:13:53.860
an invalid request preserves the last valid

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:54.216
value?

00:13:54.216 --> 00:13:57.066
Keep the interface observations and model checks

00:13:57.066 --> 00:13:57.600
distinct.
